        "original_id": "fdad3728-f247-5f3e-b716-6c7dc2ed94a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Del Davis\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Songs: \"A World Without Love\", \"World Without Love\"\n- Albums: \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist who was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop duo Peter and Gordon.\n- \"A World Without Love\" was the biggest hit of Peter and Gordon and was a No. 1 million-selling song.\n- Paul McCartney wrote \"A World Without Love,\" and the song was attributed to Lennon–McCartney.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on the album \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
